1. DEFINITIONS
"Owner" means the rights holder identified above or a lawful successor.
"NOCTYRA" means the project, including its source, object code, protocols, formats, architecture, documentation, designs, test suites, build scripts, and project assets, to the extent owned or controlled by the Owner.
"Materials" means all NOCTYRA materials made available by the Owner.
"Authorized Recipient" means a person or entity expressly authorized in a written instrument signed or otherwise approved by the Owner.
"Confidential Information" means non-public Materials and non-public information disclosed for the project, including credentials, cryptographic design, keys, vulnerability reports, unreleased capabilities, and operational procedures. It excludes information demonstrably public without breach, lawfully known without confidentiality restriction before disclosure, independently developed without use of protected information, or lawfully received from a third party without a duty of confidence.

2. NO PUBLIC LICENSE
2.1 The repository is private. Repository visibility does not grant intellectual-property rights.
2.2 No license is granted to the public by publication of a URL, invitation, issue, pull request, commit, binary, screenshot, or document.
2.3 Except for non-waivable statutory rights, no person may access, execute, reproduce, modify, adapt, create derivative works from, distribute, publish, sublicense, sell, rent, lease, host, or otherwise exploit Materials without prior express written authorization.
2.4 Repository access alone is not a software license.

3. LIMITED AUTHORIZATION
3.1 The Owner may authorize a named recipient in writing, specifying purpose, materials, permitted activities, duration, and conditions.
3.2 Unless expressly stated otherwise, authorization is limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, and revocable subject to applicable law and the written terms.
3.3 Recipients must not share credentials, invite additional users, mirror the repository, or move Materials to unapproved services.
3.4 No implied license arises from silence, review, contribution, payment, or access.

4. PERMITTED ACTIVITIES
Recipients may perform only activities expressly listed in their authorization. Permission to compile, execute, test, or modify a development copy does not authorize publication, deployment, commercialization, distribution, or third-party access.

5. RESTRICTIONS
Except where mandatory law grants a non-waivable right or the Owner grants specific written permission, recipients must not:
(a) publish, mirror, sell, sublicense, transfer, or redistribute Materials;
(b) disclose source, specifications, credentials, keys, vulnerability details, or non-public project information;
(c) remove copyright, confidentiality, attribution, or proprietary notices;
(d) use Materials to operate a hosted service or commercial offering;
(e) use Materials outside the approved purpose or environment;
(f) misrepresent NOCTYRA as certified, classified, government-approved, military-approved, audited, or endorsed;
(g) introduce malicious code, unauthorized telemetry, backdoors, or credential collection;
(h) bypass access controls or use another person's credentials;
(i) commit secrets, personal documents, recovery keys, or private user data to source control;
(j) use project access for unrelated purposes.
Nothing restricts lawful security research, protected disclosures, interoperability rights, or other non-waivable legal rights.

6. CONFIDENTIALITY
6.1 Recipients shall use Confidential Information only for the authorized purpose and protect it with at least reasonable care.
6.2 Disclosure is permitted only to individuals expressly approved by the Owner and bound by written confidentiality obligations.
6.3 Recipients shall promptly report suspected or actual unauthorized access, disclosure, loss, compromise, or misuse.
6.4 Confidential Information must not be placed in public trackers, public paste services, public AI services, personal cloud drives, or unapproved systems.
6.5 For legally compelled disclosure, recipients shall, where lawful, give advance notice and disclose only what is required.
6.6 Confidentiality obligations continue for five years after disclosure; trade secrets remain protected for as long as they qualify under applicable law.

7. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
7.1 The Owner retains all rights in Materials owned by the Owner. No ownership transfers through access.
7.2 Contributors retain rights in pre-existing materials and contributions unless a separate written assignment or license validly states otherwise.
7.3 Contributions do not automatically transfer copyright. A separate contributor agreement must establish assignment or license rights before proprietary distribution.
7.4 Contributors must identify third-party code, assets, data, and applicable license obligations.
7.5 No person may submit materials they do not have the legal right to contribute.

8. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
8.1 Third-party components remain governed by their respective licenses.
8.2 This document does not relicense third-party materials or override open-source obligations.
8.3 The Owner should maintain a dependency and license inventory and review compatibility before distribution.

9. CREDENTIALS AND SECURITY MATERIALS
9.1 Passwords, private keys, recovery secrets, signing keys, tokens, and credentials are sensitive.
9.2 Secrets must never be committed to source control or shared between individuals.
9.3 Store secrets only in approved secret-management facilities and rotate credentials when compromise is suspected.
9.4 Vulnerabilities must be reported privately through a verified contact route.
9.5 Testing is permitted only against systems expressly authorized in writing.

10. SECURITY CLAIMS
10.1 NOCTYRA is a private software project. No claim of military grade, government approval, national-security certification, formal classification, or regulated deployment suitability is made.
10.2 Strong algorithms, a private repository, and internal labels do not alone establish system security.
10.3 No claim of audit, certification, or suitability is made unless supported by a specific written assessment.

11. EXPORT AND LEGAL COMPLIANCE
Each party is responsible for laws applicable to access, use, transfer, import, export, sanctions, and disclosure. This license grants no export or government-use authorization.

12. TERM AND TERMINATION
12.1 Authorization begins and ends as stated in its written instrument.
12.2 The Owner may suspend access when reasonably necessary to protect the project or investigate compromise, subject to law.
12.3 Material breach may result in termination subject to mandatory law and agreed cure provisions.
12.4 On termination, recipients must stop use, return or delete Materials as instructed, revoke credentials, and confirm completion where reasonably requested.
12.5 Legally required retention remains subject to confidentiality.
12.6 Ownership, confidentiality, third-party rights, disclaimers, liability, and provisions intended by nature to survive shall survive termination.

