To the maximum extent permitted by law, Materials are provided "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE", without express or implied warranties, including merchantability, fitness, title, non-infringement, accuracy, availability, or security.

14. LIABILITY
To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Owner is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, exemplary, punitive, or consequential loss, including loss of data, profits, business, or goodwill. Nothing excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.

15. INDEMNITY
Where lawful, a recipient is responsible for claims and losses caused by their unauthorized use, unlawful distribution, or material breach. This does not apply to non-excludable wrongdoing by the Owner or where prohibited by law.

16. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTES
This notice does not select governing law, court, or arbitration seat. Those terms must be completed in a separate signed agreement after qualified legal review.

17. GENERAL
Amendments and additional permissions must be in writing. Invalid provisions shall be limited or severed only as necessary. Failure to enforce is not waiver. Recipients may not assign authorization without written consent. Nothing creates employment, partnership, agency, or joint venture. Mandatory statutory rights remain unaffected.

